{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And let it be</b> — the sense of \"establish it upon us\" — to set right causes and endeavors, so that there be no toil for them nor trouble in all their deeds." "And the sense of \"establish it\" — that it be whole, after the manner of: \"If YHWH does not build a house\" (Psalms 127:1)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 90, :notes {0 "'סבות ועלילות' rendered literally as 'causes and endeavors'; the referent of 'them' (הם) is unstated in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:52.444293931Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}